# Choice dialogues of the storyline payoff scenes, second batch (T-143). Compiled to zz_fs_storyline_scenes2.json.

dialogue story.band.talk
n0 piper: Exhibit A: one fiddle, one voice, a lifetime of practice. Try not to swoon.
  next n1
n1 juno: Exhibit B: three anvils, the wash bucket, and Bram, who has agreed to hit one thing. Once. Gently.
  next n2
n2 bram: Hm. One hit. I'm saving it for the end.
  next n3
n3 piper: Well? Who owns the square tonight? Take your time. Pick the fiddle.
  ? The fiddle, obviously. => r0 | flag:choice.band.piper
  ? The forge band, honestly. => r1 | flag:choice.band.juno
  ? Both, together. Loudly. => r2 | flag:choice.band.both | friend:piper,10 | friend:juno,10
r0 piper: Justice! And good taste! Juno, you were wonderful. Just less fiddle.
  expr happy
r1 juno: Okay, okay, okay! We won! Bram, we won! ...Bram? He's hitting the thing. Twice!
  expr happy
r2 piper: Together? ...That's either genius or a noise complaint. Bram, one hit. Make it count.
  emote note

dialogue story.pumpkin.dorian
n0 -: Behind the store sits a very large pumpkin. Dorian wears a very guilty face.
  next n1
n1 tilda: Dorian. Is that my prize pumpkin? I've been blaming the goats all week, out loud!
  next n2
n2 dorian: ...Borrowed. For spores. It was coming back. Eventually.
  ? Let him off gently. => r0 | flag:choice.pumpkin.dorian.kind | friend:dorian,10
  ? Ask for a proper apology. => r1 | flag:choice.pumpkin.dorian.apology
  ? Grab the heavy end. Carry it back. => r2 | flag:choice.pumpkin.dorian.help | friend:tilda,10
r0 tilda: Kindly, then. But he's on the slate for a pie. Mushrooms optional.
  expr thinking
r1 dorian: Sorry, Tilda. Truly. ...Sorry, pumpkin. You were very patient.
  emote sweat
r2 tilda: You take the heavy end, Dorian takes the guilt. I'll carry the conversation.
  expr happy

dialogue story.pumpkin.marcus
n0 -: Behind the store, Marcus stands beside a very large pumpkin with a very guilty face.
  next n1
n1 tilda: Marcus! Is that my prize pumpkin? I blamed the goats. I apologized to a goat.
  next n2
n2 marcus: ...It might be. It has a nose now.
  ? Let him off gently. => r0 | flag:choice.pumpkin.marcus.kind | friend:marcus,10
  ? He owes a proper apology. => r1 | flag:choice.pumpkin.marcus.apology
  ? Help carry the evidence back. => r2 | flag:choice.pumpkin.marcus.help | friend:tilda,10
r0 tilda: Kindly. Fine. But he owes me a pie, and I've seen him measure. It'll be exact.
  expr thinking
r1 marcus: An apology. Yes. I'm sorry, Tilda. Truly. And sorry to you, pumpkin. You deserved a plan.
  emote sweat
r2 tilda: You and Marcus take the ends. I'll walk ahead and tell everyone it was the goats.
  expr happy

dialogue story.pumpkin.felix
n0 -: Behind the store, Felix stands beside a very large pumpkin, wearing a very guilty face.
  next n1
n1 tilda: Felix. Is that my prize pumpkin? You don't even like vegetables!
  next n2
n2 felix: ...It might be. The goats were very understanding about it.
  ? Let Felix off kindly. => r0 | flag:choice.pumpkin.felix.kind | friend:felix,10
  ? Ask for a proper apology. => r1 | flag:choice.pumpkin.felix.apology
  ? Offer to carry the heavy end. => r2 | flag:choice.pumpkin.felix.help | friend:tilda,10
r0 tilda: Kindly. Fine. He owes me a pie, and if there's a fish in it, I'll know.
  expr thinking
r1 felix: An apology. Yes. I'm sorry, Tilda. Truly. ...And sorry to you, pumpkin.
  emote sweat
r2 tilda: You take the heavy end. Felix can carry the excuses. They weigh more.
  expr happy

dialogue story.cat.talk
n0 -: A small gray cat sits on your boots, perfectly satisfied, and looks up at you with the patience of a landlord.
  next n1
n1 wren: Tilda calls it Ledger. Juno says Quench. Piper swears it's Sharp. Hazel files it under Index. I say Gossip. It ignores all five equally. Rude.
  next n2
n2 wren: So. You're the one it picked. What do you call it?
  ? Ledger. Tilda's right. => r0 | flag:choice.cat.ledger
  ? Quench. Juno's right. => r1 | flag:choice.cat.quench
  ? Sharp. Piper's right. => r2 | flag:choice.cat.sharp
  ? None of those. Something new. => r3 | flag:choice.cat.new | friend:wren,10
r0 wren: Ledger. Tilda will write that on her slate. In ink. With the date.
r1 wren: Quench. Juno will make it a brass name tag, and by Friday I'll say she made two.
r2 wren: Sharp. Piper will say she was right all along, in a key of her choosing.
r3 wren: Something new? Go on, then. ...It purred. It has never purred for me. That's the one.
  expr happy
  emote heart
